AWS = Amazon Web Services

AWS is a cloud computing platform provided by Amazon.

====

Main AWS Services
Amazon EC2 – Virtual servers
Amazon S3 – Cloud storage
Amazon RDS – Managed databases
AWS Lambda – Serverless computing
Amazon SageMaker – Machine Learning and AI
Amazon Bedrock – Generative AI applications
Amazon Rekognition – Image and video analysis
Amazon Comprehend – Natural Language Processing (NLP)

====

Simple Example
Your AI/ML Project
        ↓
       AWS
        ↓
 ┌─────────────────┐
 │ SageMaker       │ → Train ML models
 │ EC2             │ → Computing power
 │ S3              │ → Store datasets
 │ Lambda          │ → Run backend code
 │ Bedrock         │ → Generative AI
 └─────────────────┘

=====

In simple words

AWS is similar to GCP.

| AWS              | Google Cloud              |
| ---------------- | ------------------------- |
| Amazon EC2       | Compute Engine            |
| Amazon S3        | Cloud Storage             |
| Amazon SageMaker | Vertex AI                 |
| AWS Lambda       | Cloud Functions           |
| Amazon Bedrock   | Vertex AI / Generative AI |


=====

AWS = Amazon's Cloud Platform
GCP = Google's Cloud Platform

AWS provides the core services for an AI/ML project, with 
Amazon SageMaker handling model training and deployment while S3 stores datasets and EC2 supplies computing power.
